WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.598
<v Leo>Ava, there are 438 items in the Atlas.

00:00:04.618 --> 00:00:06.089
<v Leo>How do I find mine?

00:00:06.109 --> 00:00:07.004
<v Ava>Two filters.

00:00:07.024 --> 00:00:09.565
<v Ava>Open the Master checklist and I'll show you.

00:00:10.215 --> 00:00:11.716
<v Ava>First, filter by wave.

00:00:11.736 --> 00:00:13.091
<v Ava>Let's pick Wave 1.

00:00:13.111 --> 00:00:16.643
<v Leo>Then by workstream, which is my team, Talent Acquisition.

00:00:16.663 --> 00:00:17.941
<v Ava>Now it's a short list.

00:00:17.961 --> 00:00:20.294
<v Ava>Open one, like Background screening.

00:00:20.944 --> 00:00:22.561
<v Ava>Set yourself as the assignee.

00:00:22.581 --> 00:00:24.905
<v Ava>Type your name and pick yourself from the list.

00:00:24.925 --> 00:00:25.549
<v Leo>Done.

00:00:25.569 --> 00:00:26.939
<v Leo>It's officially mine.

00:00:26.959 --> 00:00:28.248
<v Leo>No take-backs.

00:00:28.268 --> 00:00:32.604
<v Ava>Now set the status to Drafting and a target date you actually believe in.

00:00:32.624 --> 00:00:34.507
<v Leo>Saved for everyone, instantly.

00:00:34.527 --> 00:00:36.907
<v Leo>Goodbye, emailing the tracker around.

00:00:37.557 --> 00:00:41.517
<v Ava>Then add a note: where the document lives, what's missing, your next step.

00:00:41.537 --> 00:00:43.113
<v Leo>So not just "working on it"?

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:45.549
<v Leo>That's been my status since 2019.

00:00:45.569 --> 00:00:48.224
<v Ava>A good note means nobody has to chase you.

00:00:48.874 --> 00:00:50.888
<v Leo>How often do I need to do this?

00:00:50.908 --> 00:00:51.750
<v Ava>Every week.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.941
<v Ava>The status report is generated straight from the checklist,

00:00:54.961 --> 00:00:57.074
<v Ava>so leadership reads what you enter.

00:00:57.094 --> 00:01:00.442
<v Leo>Skip a week and the steering committee reads old news.

00:01:00.462 --> 00:01:01.461
<v Leo>Got it.

00:01:02.111 --> 00:01:02.838
<v Leo>Uh oh.

00:01:02.858 --> 00:01:04.268
<v Leo>Why is this one red?

00:01:04.288 --> 00:01:08.059
<v Ava>It's overdue: the target date has passed and the item isn't finished.

00:01:08.079 --> 00:01:10.107
<v Ava>Maybe the approver's on vacation.

00:01:10.127 --> 00:01:10.866
<v Leo>Classic.

00:01:10.886 --> 00:01:12.927
<v Leo>So do I just quietly move the date?

00:01:12.947 --> 00:01:13.913
<v Ava>Not quietly.

00:01:13.933 --> 00:01:18.446
<v Ava>Note what's blocking it, agree a new date with your workstream lead, then update it.

00:01:19.096 --> 00:01:23.068
<v Ava>Filter, open, assign yourself, update status and date, leave a note.

00:01:23.088 --> 00:01:24.039
<v Ava>Every week.

00:01:24.059 --> 00:01:26.727
<v Leo>A few minutes a week and nobody chases me?

00:01:26.747 --> 00:01:27.477
<v Leo>Sold.

00:01:27.497 --> 00:01:30.061
<v Leo>Next up, documenting a process.
